		(uuid "6c6690ce-cc3d-5de7-90d8-8c421e6245bd")
	)
	(text "Notes\n1. The Arduino is powered over USB from the experiment PC. Its 5V pin is left unconnected\n    on purpose, so the LED supply can never back-feed the PC's USB port.\n2. Arduino GND and LED supply GND are joined on this board (common ground for the data signals).\n3. R1 / R2 sit next to the Arduino and damp ringing on the long data lines.\n4. Strip wiring: LED 0 at the start of the track, both strips mounted in the same direction.\n    Use J4 to feed +5V / GND into the strips further along the track (power injection).\n5. The Nano R4 has 5 V GPIO. A 3.3 V board (e.g. Nano 33 IoT) needs a level shifter in the data lines."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 45.72 148.59 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "7cfbbe60-18c5-5d6d-8f98-f4d23469ad8e")
	)
	(text "LED strips"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 194.31 36.83 0)
		(effects
